  "name": "Mean Daily Extremes Temperature, Mean Monthly Precipitation, Mean and Extreme Sea Surface Temperature, Typhoons, and Clouds for Asia",
  "description": "Publication Title: Far East climatic atlas / prepared by Technical Services, 20th Weather Squadron. Contains summarized charts of mean daily maximum and minimum temperatures; mean monthly precipitation; mean maximum and minimum sea temperatures; percentage of time cloud cover is less than 3/10; percentage of time ceiling and visibility are 5000/5, 1000/3, and 500/2; number of days with precipitation, thunderstorm, snow, snow cover; and typhoon tracks. Data are for the Far East covering the area of 90-165 degrees E and 10-60 degrees N. Call No. QC990.A1 F3 1965 archive - available at the National Climatic Data Center Library, Asheville, North Carolina, U.S.A.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: This publication is in the National Climatic Data Center's Foreign Data Library, and is one of many books, atlases, maps, charts and other printed materials received by the NCDC from many nations over the years.",
